{"reference":"Isaiah 27","book":"Isaiah","chapter":27,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Leviathan","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Leviathan in verse 1 draws on both recognizable animal traits and larger mythopoetic, cosmic imagery. Comparisons with animals such as a crocodile are common, but the figure exceeds a simple zoological identification. The text alone does not establish that Leviathan is a dinosaur, an extinct reptile, a modern state, or the devil.","verse_refs":["Isaiah 27:1"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_027_a442b95b39f53aefdea1eebe"]}]}],"generated_metadata":null}